Revision history for Kubernetes-Comb-SVG

{{$NEXT}}

 - First release. Renders a set of Kubernetes::Comb custom resources as one
   self-contained SVG honeycomb: one hexagon per Comb, coloured by phase,
   with dependency edges and upstream (borrowed) marking.
 - Kubernetes::Comb::SVG::Cell reads a Comb custom resource (hash or TO_JSON
   object, array or List) into a cell, identified by namespace/name, with
   spec.dependsOn resolved into dependencies and missing.
 - Kubernetes::Comb::SVG::Layout places cells in groups (by name, unnamed
   last), in rows by dependency depth over all cells, on a pointy-top
   honeycomb that wraps at the column limit; dependency cycles share a row.
 - Kubernetes::Comb::SVG->render draws the honeycomb: phase-coloured hexagons,
   borrowed and disabled states, dependency edges routed through the label-free
   corners (cycles in a row bow in opposite directions) and starting at a small
   dot just inside the dependent's outline, legend, link callback, light and
   dark colour schemes.
 - theme sets phase colours and the surfaces of the picture (bg, fg, muted,
   border, edge); a value is one colour or { light => ..., dark => ... }, and
   a bad colour falls back to the default of its mode. The colours are CSS
   custom properties (--comb-*), documented with the classes as the styling
   interface.
 - blink and blink_seconds make cells of the named phases pulse through a CSS
   animation (comb-blink, no script); with prefers-reduced-motion they get a
   thicker outline instead. Without blink the SVG carries no animation CSS.
 - examples/demo.pl renders examples/demo.json (fifteen Combs in two groups,
   every phase, a borrowed and a disabled Comb) to examples/demo.svg, the
   picture the README shows; a test fails when the committed picture is stale.
 - bin/comb-svg renders Comb custom resources from a JSON file or standard
   input (a List, an array or one resource) to an SVG on standard output, with
   --title, --group-label, --columns, --size, --no-edges, --no-legend,
   --layout, --rows, --aspect, --edges, --color KEY=COLOUR or
   KEY=LIGHT,DARK (repeatable), --blink and --blink-seconds. Bad
   input or options give one line on standard error and exit status 1.
 - layout => 'packed' draws a status monitor: all Combs sorted by
   namespace/name in one compact honeycomb that fits a screen. The grid comes
   from columns, else rows, else aspect (default 16/9, measured on the whole
   canvas); edges are off unless asked for. examples/monitor.svg shows it
   (blinking for Error),
   with a freshness test, and the README too.
 - A cell name that does not fit on one line is broken into two after a
   hyphen, dot or underscore, in a smaller font when needed; only what fits
   neither way is cut with an ellipsis. Names that fit are drawn as before.
 - Stopped and NotDeployed are known phases with their own colour (teal,
   blue), legend entry, theme key, --comb-stopped / --comb-notdeployed custom
   property and blink name. The <style> block of every picture grows by these
   two.
